### Story

Glim the Gnome Warlock and his Succubus, Velvet, trekked through Stranglethorn’s steamy jungles. When a pack of ogres charged, Velvet’s Seduction froze the leader mid-swing, buying Glim time to cast Shadow Bolt. When a troll shaman tried to flee, Lesser Invisibility let Velvet stalk and Lash of Pain finish him. Between fights, Soothing Kiss kept aggro off Glim while he drank. By dusk, Glim grinned—Velvet’s control and burst made the Vale feel like a playground.

### Answer

Because Voidwalker’s threat tools (Torment, Suffering) and defensive tools (Sacrifice shield, Consume Shadows) make solo leveling safer and smoother, especially in crowded or high-damage zones. Succubus is better for burst and CC, but Voidwalker’s consistent survivability and threat management are more forgiving for most leveling scenarios. [end of text]


